usage: sandbox.py [-h] [--directory DIRECTORY] [--scope {cp,ecosystem}]
                  [--cp-service CP_SERVICE]
                  [--pm-results-service PM_RESULTS_SERVICE]
                  [--pm-locks-service PM_LOCKS_SERVICE]
                  [--cp-segment CP_SEGMENT] [--pm-segment PM_SEGMENT]
                  {up,verify,down}

Own Fury Sandbox lifecycle using installed CLI API routes, never KMS
configuration. Help/syntax checks are preparation only. Server schema,
permissions and generated Toolkit configuration must pass against the real
service before certification.

positional arguments:
  {up,verify,down}

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --directory DIRECTORY
  --scope {cp,ecosystem}
                        up defaults to ecosystem; verify/down use the receipt
                        unless explicitly constrained
  --cp-service CP_SERVICE
  --pm-results-service PM_RESULTS_SERVICE
  --pm-locks-service PM_LOCKS_SERVICE
  --cp-segment CP_SEGMENT
  --pm-segment PM_SEGMENT
